WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.942
You checked a writer register's shape,
scanned a month of audit records against it,

3
00:00:05.942 --> 00:00:08.437
and read the saved query that Gate 7 runs.

4
00:00:08.437 --> 00:00:11.014
Along the way you saw four second writers,

5
00:00:11.014 --> 00:00:14.500
one forbidden delete, and one
backstop that acted first.

6
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.424
Carry one thing forward: inbound
provisioning writes the leave

7
00:00:18.424 --> 00:00:22.125
date and the active value, and
that's true for contractors too.

8
00:00:22.125 --> 00:00:26.175
Next is Module 2: run contractors
from their own source.

9
00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:31.712
Contractors don't come from HR, and an end
date nobody updates keeps access alive.

10
00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:36.747
In Module 2 you'll compute each contractor's
earliest end, reconcile the register,

11
00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:40.579
the card system and the directory
without changing anything,

12
00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:44.930
and write a sponsor review that
removes access when nobody responds.
